Let's edit body background and remove pseudo. Use `background-color` and `background-image`. Simpler:
```
body{
...
background-color:var(--bg);
background-image: radial-gradient(...), ...;
background-attachment:fixed;
}
```
But `background-attachment:fixed` on mobile Safari can cause performance. Could use `background-attachment: scroll` and the gradients scroll with page. On long result page, gradients would stay at top only. Fixed is fine. Or use `background: var(--bg) fixed`? Let's do background-image + background-attachment fixed. That gives viewport gradient. Remove pseudo. Body background will cover. Good.

Fix badge:
```
.dial__badge{
...
background:var(--badge);color:#fff;font-weight:...
border:5px solid var(--surface);
box-shadow: 0 8px 18px ..., inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.25);
}
```
Remove `::before`. Width 56 includes border; inner 46. At 980 width 48 inner 38, still good. Maybe use `border:4px solid var(--surface)` to keep letters. At 48, inner 40. Good. `box-sizing:border-box` global. Fine.
- With border surface, it looks like a bead on ring. Good.
- `.dial__badge` color white. Good.

Fix h1 em:
```
isolation:isolate
```
and pseudo z-index -1 still behind text but within em. Good.

